}∼N(2, 7)$ and $X_{2}∼N(1, 4)$ are independent and $Y = 2X_{1} - 3X_{2}$, calculate $P(-4.6 < Y < 3.48)$. Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$$0.00$$0.01$$0.02$$0.03$$0.04$$0.2$ $0.5793$ $0.5832$ $0.5871$ $0.5910$ $0.5948$ $0.3$ $0.6179$ $0.6217$ $0.6255$ $0.6293$ $0.6331$ $0.4$ $0.6554$ $0.6591$ $0.6628$ $0.6664$ $0.6700$ |  | $z$$0.00$$0.01$$0.02$$0.03$$-0.7$ $0.2420$ $0.2389$ $0.2358$ $0.2327$ $-0.6$ $0.2743$ $0.2709$ $0.2676$ $0.2643$ $-0.5$ $0.3085$ $0.3050$ $0.3015$ $0.2981$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162061 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22f7e940-b159-5d68-8ce4-d33f4a2f6907" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Probability Involving a Sum or Difference of Normally Distributed Random Variables in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b869df3-79ba-56aa-8ced-f8b4ad215428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9826" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158985} {:answer/id #uuid "b8003671-7ca0-5043-9de3-be6566db4166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9783" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158986} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0e5659-7545-58cd-9efa-736e9883e318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9713" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158987} {:answer/id #uuid "08ac1861-7dd0-5294-a3e1-01ada62d50d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9732" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158988} {:answer/id #uuid "686c79f7-f1c1-5bde-b527-10584fabc17c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9838" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158989}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6523aa17-ab8d-5913-92fd-b0f4e669d487" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158984}] :question/id #uuid "6e40bec4-6131-5212-9aba-bedf95289725" :question/math-academy-id "q-110340" :question/problem "A shop sells spray foam in small and large cans. The volume of liquid in a small can is normally distributed with a mean of $0.3ltrs$ and a standard deviation of $0.003ltrs$. The volume of liquid in a large can is normally distributed with a mean of $0.6ltrs$ and a standard deviation of $0.008ltrs$.\n\nThe foam from a small can expands $40$ times its liquid volume after being sprayed in place, while the foam from a large can expands to $60$ times its liquid volume.\nIf one small and one large can are randomly selected, what is the probability that the total foam volume from both cans after expanding is less than $49ltrs$?\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$ | $0.00$ | $0.01$ | $0.02$ | $0.03$ | $0.04$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1.9$ | $0.9713$ | $0.9719$ | $0.9726$ | $0.9732$ | $0.9738$ |\n| $2.0$ | $0.9772$ | $0.9778$ | $0.9783$ | $0.9788$ | $0.9793$ |\n| $2.1$ | $0.9821$ | $0.9826$ | $0.9830$ | $0.9834$ | $0.9838$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
